	affiliations = {Department of Chemistry, University of Cambridge, Cambridge, CB2 1EW, Lensfield Road, United Kingdom},
	abstract = {The effect of the argon atom on the magnetic shielding tensor at the proton and fluorine nuclei in Ar···HF has been studied by SCF/GIAO ab initio computation and by a classical model. The long-range classical model, which includes the electric and magnetic terms, gives good agreement for the change of the H shielding anisotropy. The magnetic term dominates the H shielding change; the electric field and field gradient contributions to the electric term are of opposite sign. At the experimental intermolecular distance, the change in the isotropic proton shielding (Formula presented.) is −0.3 ppm and in the anisotropy δ(Δσ) = δ(σVerbar;—σ∉) it is 6.6 ppm. This large increase in the anisotropy arises from the magnetizability of the Ar atom and the linearity of the F—H···Ar bond. © 1999 Taylor & Francis Group, LLC.},
